# Web Scanner
# Description: Flags a client IP that receives many 403/404 responses in one 5-minute bin, a sign of path fuzzing.
# ATT&CK: T1595.003 (Active Scanning: Wordlist Scanning)
# Severity: Low
# Schedule: Every 5 minutes, search window earliest=-10m latest=now
# Threshold: count >= 20 responses with status 403 or 404 from one clientip in a 5-minute bin
# Known false positives: Search engine crawlers hitting stale URLs; a broken internal link hammered by users;
#   monitoring probes pointed at removed pages.
# Index: tutorial

index=tutorial sourcetype=access_combined* status IN (403, 404)
| bin _time span=5m
| stats count by _time, clientip
| where count >= 20
| sort -_time
